= Recovery Legislation

With unified control we can pass a major recovery package using the budget reconciliation process. The economy is still recovering and the virus is not yet beaten.

- @rescue_big: A huge package ($1.9 trillion)
- @rescue_mid: A moderate package
- @rescue_small: A targeted, minimal bill

@rescue_big
on-arrival: stimulus_level += 2; economic_growth += 2; unemployed -= 0.8; inflation += 1; budget -= 2; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 3; moderate_dissent += 2

Checks go out and the child tax credit expands. The economy booms, and prices begin to climb.

@rescue_mid
on-arrival: stimulus_level += 1; economic_growth += 1; unemployed -= 0.4; inflation += 0.3; budget -= 1; moderate_strength += 2; progressive_dissent += 2

A smaller package passes with a bipartisan flavor.

@rescue_small
on-arrival: economic_growth += 0.3; budget += 1; progressive_dissent += 6; working_dem -= 1*(1-dissent)

We pare back. The recovery is slow.
